From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:45:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the CPU dynamic power
 coefficients

With dynamic-power-coefficient on the CPUs, cpufreq-dt registers an
Energy Model for both clusters from their operating points, and the
scheduler can place tasks by energy: the capacities are asymmetric
(capacity-dmips-mhz 454 and 1024) and both clusters have cpufreq.

Set 170 on the six Cortex-A55 and 512 on the two Cortex-A76 cores.
They come from a fit of wall power against frequency on one board and
are not calibrated; the loss of the power supply is in both values and
cancels in their ratio, which is what the scheduler compares. The
vendor BSP uses 162 and 598.

Not covered: whether the values suit this board. The patch makes no
claim of its own about performance or energy and can be dropped alone.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the Energy Model is
created for both clusters with the coefficients as set, 170 on the A55
cores and 512 on the A76 cores, and the power of every state agrees with
its coefficient and the voltage of the board's bin.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 2035741da74b..4b9746f011ee 100644
